#: lib/tymeslot_saas_web/live/feature_live/pages/self_hosting.ex:33
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Most scheduling tools are closed SaaS: your availability, your clients' names and emails, and your connected calendar tokens all live on someone else's servers, priced per seat and subject to terms that change without you. For a solo professional that is an annoyance. For a clinic, a law firm, or anyone handling regulated or sensitive data, it is a compliance problem you cannot wave away.\n\nTymeslot takes the opposite stance. The core product is open source and self-hostable end to end — there is no crippled community edition and no feature held back behind a hosted-only wall. Point it at your own PostgreSQL database, put it behind your own domain, and it behaves exactly like the managed version, because it is the same code. The server is yours, your clients' data stays on it, and you decide when to upgrade."
msgstr ""

